      "id": "029bllp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Levels of Organization in the Human Body"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The human body is structured hierarchically starting from cellular levels of organization up to complex body systems.",
        "Key body systems including the Digestive, Circulatory, Respiratory, and Excretory systems maintain metabolic homeostasis.",
        "Structural support, body movement, and protection are provided by the Skeletal and Muscular systems.",
        "Control, regulation, and body reproduction are managed by the Nervous, Endocrine, and Reproductive systems."
      ],
      "id": "fruw1hm"
    },
